ok 3 - a malformed contentTypeId is 400 INVALID_REQUEST [P2-S09-AC-139]
ok 4 - a malformed versionId is 400 INVALID_REQUEST [P2-S09-AC-139]
ok 5 - a label (the type key) cannot stand in for an identifier: it is an unknown member [P2-S09-AC-139]
ok 6 - a version that does not belong to the named type is NOT_FOUND [P2-S09-AC-139]
ok 7 - a query member is refused: the route has no query [P2-S09-AC-140]
ok 8 - a limit member is refused: the route has no limit [P2-S09-AC-140]
ok 9 - a body member is refused: the route has no body [P2-S09-AC-140]
ok 10 - a idempotency key member is refused: the route has no idempotency key [P2-S09-AC-140]
ok 11 - a If-Match member is refused: the route has no If-Match [P2-S09-AC-140]
ok 12 - a expected version member is refused: the route has no expected version [P2-S09-AC-140]
ok 13 - a artifact flag member is refused: the route has no artifact flag [P2-S09-AC-140]
ok 14 - the server correlation id is the one extra member admitted beside the context [P2-S09-AC-140]
ok 15 - a verified schema designer of the owning scope reads the detail [P2-S09-AC-141]
ok 16 - an authenticated human with neither registry-read nor designer scope is 403 FORBIDDEN [P2-S09-AC-142]
ok 17 - another organization's designer gets an indistinguishable 404 for a real version [P2-S09-AC-142]
ok 18 - and the same 404 for an absent version, so the two cannot be told apart [P2-S09-AC-142]
ok 19 - the concealed and the absent responses are both empty [P2-S09-AC-142]
ok 20 - and carry no differing detail [P2-S09-AC-142]
ok 21 - the other organization reads its own version [P2-S09-AC-141]
ok 22 - an acting context the human is not bound to is refused: the acting context is rechecked, never widened [P2-S09-AC-141]
|||{"role": "service_role"}
ok 23 - no verified actor is 401 UNAUTHENTICATED [P2-S09-AC-141]
ok 24 - the detail RPC is executable by the authenticated role and never by anon: the RLS-bound read is the only public-facing entry [P2-S09-AC-141]
ok 25 - the tables the detail reads have forced RLS and no direct browser privilege, so RLS and the acting context are the recheck [P2-S09-AC-141]
ok 26 - control: the detail is read again for the projection checks [P2-S09-AC-144]
ok 27 - the detail always includes the capability-safe artifact identity and hash [P2-S09-AC-144]
ok 28 - the artifact projection is exactly the identity, hash, compiler, contract reference, state and timestamps: no manifest body [P2-S09-AC-144]
ok 29 - no optional artifact flag exists in the read [P2-S09-AC-144]
ok 30 - the detail projects the two registered blocks [P2-S09-AC-145]
ok 31 - each block is the safe registry record: identity, lifecycle, release digest, props reference and hash, renderer [P2-S09-AC-145]
ok 32 - no block carries the snapshot, attestation, release keys, body or nonce hashes, verification timestamps, source or executable evidence [P2-S09-AC-145]
ok 33 - each block carries the lifecycle derived from its events [P2-S09-AC-145]
ok 34 - the other organization reads its own detail [P2-S09-AC-145]
ok 35 - blocks are platform registry records, not tenant data: the same two safe records are visible to an authorized reader of any organization [P2-S09-AC-145]
ok 36 - no private control-plane payload, release evidence or ownership member enters the detail [P2-S09-AC-146]
ok 37 - the detail and list read no public delivery table [P2-S09-AC-146]
ok 38 - neither projection function contains a write, an idempotency reservation, an audit or outbox call or a row lock [P2-S09-AC-184]
ok 39 - a successful detail read changes no definition, migration, idempotency, audit, outbox, lease or job row [P2-S09-AC-147]
ok 40 - a NOT_FOUND read changes nothing [P2-S09-AC-147]
ok 41 - a FORBIDDEN read changes nothing [P2-S09-AC-147]
ok 42 - an INVALID_REQUEST read changes nothing [P2-S09-AC-147]
ok 43 - a concealed read changes nothing [P2-S09-AC-147]
ok 44 - the detail refuses a request with no identifiers and changes nothing [P2-S09-AC-184]
ok 45 - a successful list changes no definition, migration, idempotency, audit, outbox, lease or job row [P2-S09-AC-184]
ok 46 - a failed list changes nothing either [P2-S09-AC-184]
ok 47 - the projection RPCs are VOLATILE SECURITY DEFINER, so their read-only behavior is the property proved above, not a planner promise [P2-S09-AC-184]
